Switch Frame Tap is an independent upstream project by Tomas Uribe:
https://github.com/TomasUribe/switch-frame-tap

The upstream viewer source is not included in this repository. The installer
downloads the pinned source archive and verifies its SHA256 before applying
the Pi patches. The upstream project and its source retain their own copyright
and license notices.

The pi-switch-dock scripts, boot configuration helper, tests, documentation
and patches are distributed under GNU GPL version 2 only (GPL-2.0-only).
See LICENSE for the full license text. Upstream copyright notices remain
with the downloaded source. This repository distributes source and a patch,
not prebuilt receiver executables.

The Pi patches add V4L2 M2M hardware decoding, fullscreen startup, low-latency
DRM scanout, frame pacing, HDMI mode selection and a visible build version.
Patch headers identify the modified upstream files and carry modification
notices dated 2026-11-03. The patches are GPL-2.0-only.

